<title>INDIA: Indian soybean quiet in lacklustre trade.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean quiet in lacklustre trade.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian market on Tuesday with some markets closed for a local holiday. Arrivals were around 8,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent prices were slightly up due to better demand. Soyoil solvent rose 100 rupees per tonne. Soyoil refined was steady. The undertone was dull as selling pressure was high. Business was light.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices remained bearish as export demand was poor. Soymeal yellow was $265 per tonne in export while rapeseed extraction was quoted at $135. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,550-4,575 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
